  "summary": "Four recent preprints revisit accidental and topological bound states in the continuum across resonator, lattice and metasurface platforms.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the characterization of bound states in the continuum (BICs) in open photonic systems, where localized modes persist within the radiation continuum. Two items address accidental BICs directly. One shows that accidental BICs in vertically asymmetric photonic lattices are governed by radiation-source parity and are recovered through radiation-source parity restoration. The other models metasurface BICs as converging reflection and transmission zeros and argues that accidental BICs require spatially nonlocal response. A third study examines Berry phase and topological quasi-bound states in Möbius resonators, reporting that the phase depends on mode. The fourth treats a self-dual spectral singularity in coupled gain and loss ring resonators coupled to a waveguide, a related scattering-singularity problem rather than a BIC study. The new element across the set is the framing of accidental BIC existence in terms of parity and nonlocality.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
